Runtime dependencies and outputs
--------------------------------

The documented FastWAM implementation resolves the listed model components at
exact revisions chosen by the workflow. Their public Apache-2.0 model-card
licenses were inspected for this recipe, but no component byte is redistributed
by this image. Dataset, cache, checkpoint and output terms are separate from the
source/model notice: the operator supplies the dataset's authoritative license,
and generated checkpoint artifacts may contain runtime model components. Keep
those run outputs private unless their complete downstream redistribution
closure is independently established. Access to a public endpoint does not
change any upstream use or redistribution terms.

The Wan model cards additionally say that Wan claims no rights over generated
content, while placing responsibility for compliant use and non-harmful sharing
on the user. This provenance record preserves that upstream statement; it does
not create an NPA click-through, acceptance variable, or additional EULA.

NPA modifications
-----------------

NPA adds an orchestration adapter only: episode-disjoint data receipt, native
``lerobot-train`` / ``lerobot-eval`` execution, direct-action latency measurement,
and factual MP4/RRD provenance. It does not relabel upstream FastWAM research as
NPA work and does not implement the separate Cosmos3 FastWAM-K2 experiment.
